WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.110
- Babka is beautiful,
tasty, comforting, sweet,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.100
family, love, home.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.160
It's basically life to me.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.660
Hi, my name is Chef Shimi,

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.805
and today I'm gonna teach you

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:15.200
how to make a show stopping babka.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.980
To get started, we'll make our dough.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.110
First we're gonna place

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.660
all the dried ingredients in a mixer bowl.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.110
We're gonna mix all the
dry ingredients together.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.100
Then put it on a standing mixer.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.880
We don't have to use a standing mixer,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.430
we can do it by hand,

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.730
but it's gonna take much more time.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.010
We need the dough hook

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.460
because that's the one you're
using for bread kneading.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.599
We'll attach the hook,

00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:39.870
and then we'll add the water.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.870
Our water is gonna be a little warm,

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.770
between 95 and 100 degrees.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.370
It needs to be that temperature

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:50.930
in order to help activate
the yeast much quicker.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.980
If it's too hot it can kill the yeast,

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.210
and we don't want that.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.270
So we'll turn the mixer
on speed number two,

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.920
and we're gonna start
mixing all the ingredients.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.350
We're gonna add a teaspoon of vanilla.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.890
I do vanilla just to get some
more aroma into the dough,

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:07.860
and more flavor.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.810
And I just like the smell
of it when you're baking.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.840
One egg and a quarter cup of oil.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.620
The reason I use oil instead of butter

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.640
is because of the way my mom was baking.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.750
We knead the dough for
about seven to 10 minutes.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.400
It just needs to become smooth,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.360
and all the ingredients
need to incorporate.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.680
Ours is looking a little bit dry,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.240
so I'll add one tablespoon of water.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.410
It's coming together,

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:36.870
and the sign that it's
all been incorporated

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.980
is the fact that the mixer bowl is clean.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.130
I like to remove it from the mixer bowl,

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:43.800
and then put it on a surface,

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.010
and start kneading it
by hand just a tiny bit,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.990
just to get a feel of it,

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:52.090
and to be in more control of the dough.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:55.540
One of my favorite parts
is to knead by hand.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.990
By babka journey started in London,

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:01.990
and from there I started baking every day,

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.260
and started getting people
contacting me for it,

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.100
posting it on social media.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.750
People wanted to buy it from me.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.900
Then I started traveling in Europe,

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.130
teaching students how
to make their own babka.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.750
So the babka we make today
is not a traditional babka,

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.490
but it's my interpretation
of what I wanted it to be.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.520
So we shape it with our hands,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.570
and we're turning it into a smooth ball.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.730
And then we get a mixing
bowl sprayed with oil,

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.040
and we place it in the bowl,

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.470
and then we wrap it with
cling film or plastic wrap.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:38.180
We let the dough rise for
about 45 minutes to an hour.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.608
While we wait for the dough to rise,

00:02:39.608 --> 00:02:41.730
we're going to make our filling.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.600
I liked to roast the hazelnuts

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.690
because it takes the oil out of it,

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.610
and creates more flavor and more texture.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:49.770
We place them on the pan,

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.943
and then we roast them
for about eight minutes.

00:02:52.943 --> 00:02:55.490
We'll put these in the food processor,

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.860
and then mix them until
they're nicely chopped.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.240
You want a consistency

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.660
that wouldn't be too much of a powder,

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.960
but still has some texture to it.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.840
Now we're going to make
the chocolate ganache.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.400
I prefer doing the chocolate
ganache from scratch

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.510
'cause I believe it tastes much better.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:12.310
First of all we're gonna melt the butter.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:14.020
I use butter instead of cream

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.420
because it's less heavy,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.420
and because it makes the
layers look more distinct.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.050
And as soon as the
butter melted completely

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.040
we're gonna add the chocolate to it,

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.320
and start whisking is slowly.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.450
When the two are incorporated,

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.230
we're going to add the cocoa powder

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.370
and start whisking until it all dissolves.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.880
Then we add the powdered sugar,

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.190
which is the last thing for the ganache,

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.680
and we keep whisking it

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.010
until we don't see any lumps.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.390
We're looking for a
spreadable consistency,

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.614
nothing too runny or too thick.

00:03:47.614 --> 00:03:49.190
Our ganache is ready,

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.410
so we'll set it aside

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.690
and start making our syrup.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.210
Babka always has syrup,

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.160
but I kind of made mine a
little bit less traditional.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.060
To get started,

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.390
we're going to peel the
skin from the orange.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.160
I like to use a pairing knife.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.740
So we're gonna hold the
orange in the center,

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.510
and then starting from the top,

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.840
going towards the bottom,

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:09.800
we're gonna peel it using the knife.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.760
After doing that we're gonna
start chopping the orange peel.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.890
I like to chop it really fine,

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.950
but you can do it the way you wanna do it.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.280
It doesn't have to be perfect.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:20.650
Orange peel is really untraditional.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.250
It reminds me of my childhood

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:25.420
when I used to make
candied orange with my mom,

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.130
and we used to dip it in chocolate.

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:28.180
I love oranges,

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.840
and I incorporate in almost
everything that I do.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.100
So first of all we're
gonna boil the water,

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.840
and as soon as they're boiling

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.850
we're gonna add the sugar,

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.860
and make sure it dissolves properly.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.480
Keep stirring it for about three minutes,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.940
and then add the cinnamon stick

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.280
and star anise.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.800
Mix it a little bit
more for about a minute.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.870
And add the orange peel to it.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.500
I love aromas.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.510
Star anise is very middle eastern,

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:53.440
as well as cinnamon.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.410
I grew up in Israel.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.720
My family originated in the middle east,

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.500
so this syrup is an homage to my family

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.980
and my heritage.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.990
It just reminds me of my childhood,

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.640
and everything that I used
to love and still love.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.010
So we wanna cook the syrup
with the orange peel in it

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.960
for about 20-25 minutes.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.510
We want to get a thicker consistency,

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.503
but we also wanna cook the peels through.

00:05:17.503 --> 00:05:20.180
Let's set it aside and
get back to our dough.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:21.600
Our dough doubled in size.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.433
It looks great.

00:05:22.433 --> 00:05:23.710
We can remove the plastic now,

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.990
and take out some of the air.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.150
I love punching the dough

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.820
'cause it's a fun thing to do.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.790
So we'll punch the
dough, get some air out,

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.780
start making it more smooth on the sides,

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.710
turn it into a firm bowl again,

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.480
and set it on the surface.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:38.950
And then we'll slice it in half.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:40.600
This recipe makes two loaves.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.510
If you have guests this
is the perfect dessert.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:44.350
Every time I make it,

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.670
'cause I practice so much,

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:46.960
and I bake so much,

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.590
my neighbors are always the ones

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:51.310
who are enjoying more than anyone else,

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.900
'cause I knock on people's
doors with babkas,

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:57.000
and just love to give them as a gift,

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.090
'cause I think they make everyone happy.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.680
We start working with
one piece of the dough.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.926
We sprinkle some flour on a surface,

00:06:04.926 --> 00:06:09.080
and using a rolling pin
we start rolling the dough

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.280
from top to bottom,

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.040
and then over to the sides

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.420
into a rectangle sized 21 by 15 inches.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.850
So now it's time to bring the beautiful

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.570
and smooth chocolate ganache,

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:21.970
and start spreading it on the dough.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:25.520
I love to use a silicone spatula for that

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.230
'cause I feel the metal
ones can hurt the dough

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.750
and pinch it, so that's my best tip.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.760
After we spread the
chocolate on the dough,

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.800
and we make sure it's spread evenly,

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:37.290
because we want everyone
to get the same bite

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.500
when they eat the babka.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.741
Then we use the hazelnut,

00:06:40.741 --> 00:06:44.650
and we sprinkle it evenly
all over the chocolate.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:49.260
The next thing we'll do
is start turning the dough

00:06:50.581 --> 00:06:51.414
into a log.

00:06:51.414 --> 00:06:52.350
We're gonna work lengthwise.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.680
So from bottom to top

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.300
we're gonna start rolling it,

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.360
and pressing it very gently

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.140
just to make sure it stays.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.130
The reason we wanna get the tight spiral

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:02.860
is because we wanna be able

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.080
to see these beautiful layers at the end.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.570
After you finished rolling the two logs,

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.400
you let them rest for 15 minutes

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.870
before we slice them.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.036
Have a drink, relax.

00:07:12.036 --> 00:07:13.620
There's a babka coming.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.453
So it's rested,

00:07:14.453 --> 00:07:15.900
and now it's ready to be cut.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:18.670
We are going to use a serrated knife,

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.410
and the reason being is because,

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.600
again, we don't wanna hurt
and damage the babka inside,

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.550
and we wanna keep those beautiful layers.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.720
So we'll do it very, very gently,

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.440
and slice it without pressing the dough.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.150
Look at those layers.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.870
That's exactly what we want.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.103
Now we're gonna braid.

00:07:37.433 --> 00:07:40.470
We're going to place one on
top of the other in an S shape,

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:42.590
and then starting from the center

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:45.570
we're gonna start braiding
it from the center

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.010
over to the bottom,

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.170
and from the center over to the top.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.024
If you wanna do the traditional one,

00:07:51.024 --> 00:07:52.610
you can just leave it like this,

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:54.130
and bake it just like the loaf,

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.710
but if you wanna make my classic round,

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:57.830
you do the same braid,

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.260
but you're gonna spiral it.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:00.790
Today we're gonna do the wreath shape

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.520
because I think it's a show stopper,

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.900
and it's suitable for the holiday season.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.110
So when it's rounded,

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:07.980
we'll place it in a round baking dish.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.710
We're adding egg wash
to give it some color

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.630
and to create some more
strength to the dough.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.740
I don't like to use a lot

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.130
because I don't like pastries

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.934
that looks like there's
an omelet on top of it.

00:08:16.934 --> 00:08:18.803
This is why I dilute it

00:08:18.803 --> 00:08:20.640
with just a little bit of water.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.410
So I add one tablespoon of
water on each egg that I use.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.750
And then using a brush

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:28.300
I just brush it really, really gently,

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:29.960
you don't wanna have too much egg on it

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.630
because it's just gonna hide
the beauty of the babka.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:36.510
We're baking this for
about 25 to 30 minutes.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.930
Our wreath is ready, it looks beautiful.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.860
It's golden brown all around, gorgeous.

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:45.050
So now while it's still hot
we wanna soak it with syrup.

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:46.440
They both need to be hot

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:50.080
in order for the syrup
to soak into the babka

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:52.030
and create the texture we wanna create.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.420
This is my favorite, favorite part

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:55.730
of making babka,

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:57.560
which is the decoration part

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:58.730
and the garnishing.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:00.792
We're going to use rose petals,

00:09:00.792 --> 00:09:04.060
they remind me scents from my childhood.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.150
They remind me of home.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.660
And I like to add pistachios

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.736
because I love the flavor,

00:09:07.736 --> 00:09:09.690
but I also love the colors.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.030
Finally it's ready, we can eat it.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.306
Cut me a slice already.

00:09:13.306 --> 00:09:15.160
This is the surprise.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.440
I like slicing it,

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:19.810
and then you see all of these
beautiful swirls inside.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.830
This is the most satisfying part.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.260
If you end up making this,

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.660
and it doesn't look like that,

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.450
that's fine, it's still
gonna taste delicious,

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.810
just keep practicing.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:31.550
Visual is something that
will happen eventually,

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:32.950
you just have to keep doing it.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.190
Thank you guys so much,

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.290
I hope you make it

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:36.360
and enjoy it.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.630
And if you do, please
take a picture of it,

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.543
tag me in it because I love seeing

00:09:41.543 --> 00:09:44.368
what you guys are doing with it.

00:09:44.368 --> 00:09:47.035
(gentle music)

